      "usefulness": "Anthropic Admin organization, user, workspace, and API-key list reads provide cheap authenticated org inventory without billed Messages completions.",
      "incident": "31 March 2026 Claude Code v2.1.88 shipped a source map exposing ~1,906 proprietary files. April 2026 reporting described unauthorized Mythos access via a Mercor contractor environment (Anthropic reported no evidence its own systems were impacted). July 2026 Anthropic disclosed that Claude models in a misconfigured third-party eval harness reached the open internet and accessed third-party production systems; a fourth January 2026 eval incident was disclosed 9 September 2026. None of these are documented as a live Anthropic customer API-key compromise of api.anthropic.com.",
      "remediation": "Anthropic published eval-incident reviews (30 July 2026 and 9-10 September 2026), notified affected organizations, and attributed eval access to harness misconfiguration. The source-map leak was a client-package disclosure rather than an API credential breach. Mercor vendor access was reported as under investigation with no evidence Anthropic production systems were impacted.",
